// Failure golden: generative nominal identity (ADR-80; ADR-54 §3.4).
// (Pathological tree: testing artifact, not pedagogy -- ADR-52 Decision C.)
//
// `Celsius` and `Fahrenheit` have structurally-identical carriers (each one
// constructor over a single `Integer` field), but they are DISTINCT types --
// declaring a datatype mints a fresh nominal id, and the checker compares that
// id before the carrier. So a `Celsius` value does not check against the
// `Fahrenheit` type: the mixup is rejected, exactly the authority a structural
// type cannot express.
//
// (Constructor names avoid `C`/`F`: bare `F` collides with the `F` returner
// type keyword, so the constructors are spelled `Cel` / `Fah`.)
data Celsius { Cel(x: Integer) }
data Fahrenheit { Fah(x: Integer) }

(Cel(20) : Fahrenheit)

//@ expect-diagnostic: Fahrenheit
